course: dictionary
lesson: 9805
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. Swallow can be a doing word (a verb), a naming word (a noun), or both. The sentence around it tells you which meaning is used. Always ask: what does this word do, or what is it?
explain: «Roisin wants the floor to swallow her» does not mean the floor eats her. Roisin is so embarrassed that she wishes she could disappear. Try your meaning in the sentence to check it makes sense.
explain: «Swallow your pride» is a phrase. It means to put your pride aside and not show it, which is a way of hiding a feeling. When swallow is a noun, as in «a swallow», it names a small bird.
fact: Swallow as a verb means to make food, drink or something else go down your throat into your stomach.
fact: Swallow can also mean to move your throat as if swallowing, for example when you are nervous.
fact: As a noun, a swallow is a small bird with long pointed wings and a forked tail. It flies fast and catches insects.
fact: «Swallowed» means it went down your throat, as in «A swallowed button battery can burn through the throat in about two hours», so it is always an emergency.
fact: If a small child swallows a coin, a battery or medicine, tell an adult at once.
exercise: «A swallowed button battery can burn through the throat in about two hours.» What does swallowed mean here? | Chewed very slowly | Flew away fast | Hidden under the bed | *Went down the throat
exercise: «True science: swallows feed on flying insects, and in a British winter there are almost none.» What is a swallow in this sentence? | A kind of insect | A hard sweet | A gulp of water | *A small bird that catches insects
exercise: Roisin's friend whispers, «Is your house always like this?» Roisin wants the floor to swallow her. What does swallow mean? | She wants to lie down on the floor | She wants to eat the floor | She wants to drink the carpet | *She wants to vanish because she is embarrassed
test: «Swallow your pride and say sorry.» What does swallow mean in this sentence? | To eat it up | To sing loudly | To drink quickly | *To put your pride aside and not show it
test: Why do swallows fly to Africa every autumn? | Because they like the sea | Because they are chasing the sun | *Because a British winter has almost no flying insects to eat | Because they want to sleep for the winter
exam: In «A swallow built a nest under the roof», what kind of word is swallow? | *A noun | An adverb | An adjective | A verb
